WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.299 --> 00:00:06.030
A team of archaeologists uncovers a giant
ceramic vase in the ruins of an ancient Greek

00:00:06.030 --> 00:00:07.030
city.

00:00:07.030 --> 00:00:10.420
They carefully brush away the sand and debris
that surrounds it.

00:00:10.420 --> 00:00:15.020
The head archaeologist grabs a ladder and
places it gently against the 8-foot tall vase.

00:00:15.020 --> 00:00:18.599
“I am going to see if there is anything
inside,” he says.

00:00:18.599 --> 00:00:22.859
The archaeologist climbs the ladder and peers
over the lip of the ceramic vase.

00:00:22.859 --> 00:00:25.019
The inside is completely black.

00:00:25.019 --> 00:00:28.480
“I can’t see anything!” he shouts down
to the rest of the team.

00:00:28.480 --> 00:00:32.279
He reaches his arm into the pot to see if
he can feel anything.

00:00:32.279 --> 00:00:35.519
A couple of seconds later he releases a yelp
of pain.

00:00:35.519 --> 00:00:37.829
“Something bit me!” he yells.

00:00:37.829 --> 00:00:41.410
The archaeologist pulls his hand out of the
darkness and climbs down the ladder.

00:00:41.410 --> 00:00:42.980
“Is there an animal inside?”

00:00:42.980 --> 00:00:45.140
a fellow archaeologist asks.

00:00:45.140 --> 00:00:50.160
But before the question can be answered, the
ceramic vase begins to shake.

00:00:50.160 --> 00:00:54.620
Thousands of tiny creatures resembling a rat
mixed with a pug flood out of the top of the

00:00:54.620 --> 00:00:55.620
vase.

00:00:55.620 --> 00:00:58.210
They start clawing and biting the archaeologists.

00:00:58.210 --> 00:01:00.859
The men run away screaming in terror.

00:01:00.859 --> 00:01:05.690
Many are consumed by the wave of creatures;
others are overwhelmed as they try to scramble

00:01:05.690 --> 00:01:07.940
up the ruins to safety.

00:01:07.940 --> 00:01:12.860
Only minutes after the lead archaeologist
stuck his hand into the ceramic vase the screams

00:01:12.860 --> 00:01:14.120
are silenced.

00:01:14.120 --> 00:01:17.760
The creatures wander aimlessly around the
ancient Greek city.

00:01:17.760 --> 00:01:22.290
The SCP Foundation hears of the incident and
sends a team to investigate.

00:01:22.290 --> 00:01:26.920
They classify the anomalous vase as SCP-019.

00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:30.500
When they arrive on the scene, the thousands
of creatures that were manifested from the

00:01:30.500 --> 00:01:32.090
vase are found dead.

00:01:32.090 --> 00:01:39.080
These entities are designated SCP-019-2 and
incinerated before any tourists visiting the

00:01:39.080 --> 00:01:41.680
archaeological site see the corpses.

00:01:41.680 --> 00:01:44.750
The extraction team examines the vase itself.

00:01:44.750 --> 00:01:49.220
It seems like a normal, although very large,
ceramic from antiquity.

00:01:49.220 --> 00:01:54.750
The scientists put in charge of securing SCP-019
are Doctor Light and Doctor Vaux.

00:01:54.750 --> 00:01:56.530
“Be careful,” Light says.

00:01:56.530 --> 00:02:00.260
“We don’t know what the connection is
between the vase and these creatures.

00:02:00.260 --> 00:02:04.220
It seems as if they came out of it, but our
instruments aren’t detecting anything inside,

00:02:04.220 --> 00:02:07.610
and there is no way they could have all fit
into that thing anyway.”

00:02:07.610 --> 00:02:12.230
Doctor Vaux who is closely examining the vase
comes to the same conclusion.

00:02:12.230 --> 00:02:17.390
They take a step back as the extraction team
prepares to put ropes in place to move SCP-019.

00:02:17.390 --> 00:02:22.910
A rope is thrown over the vase; part of it
lands on top of the lip.

00:02:22.910 --> 00:02:27.630
Instantly an instance of SCP-019-2 appears
from the ceramic.

00:02:27.630 --> 00:02:32.010
It begins running around, clawing and biting
anything it can, but is eventually captured

00:02:32.010 --> 00:02:33.470
by Doctor Vaux.

00:02:33.470 --> 00:02:36.160
“Well, now we know where the creatures came
from.

00:02:36.160 --> 00:02:40.370
We will bring it back to the lab for further
study,” the doctor says as he hands the

00:02:40.370 --> 00:02:42.490
creature off to one of the agents.

00:02:42.490 --> 00:02:46.830
The ropes are secured and the team begins
to move the vase, but with every movement,

00:02:46.830 --> 00:02:50.790
another SCP-019-2 instance appears from the
artifact.

00:02:50.790 --> 00:02:54.180
“This is going to get really annoying,”
says Doctor Light.

00:02:54.180 --> 00:02:58.070
“Let’s put the whole damn thing in a mobile
containment chamber and let those little creatures

00:02:58.070 --> 00:03:00.740
run on top of each other rather than us chasing
them around.”

00:03:00.740 --> 00:03:03.250
“Agreed,” replies Vaux.

00:03:03.250 --> 00:03:04.691
A containment pod is brought in.

00:03:04.691 --> 00:03:12.791
The team quickly moves SCP-019 into it as
instance after instance of SCP-019-2 manifest

00:03:12.791 --> 00:03:13.930
from the vase.

00:03:13.930 --> 00:03:16.030
The doors to the pod are sealed.

00:03:16.030 --> 00:03:20.569
Light and Vaux watch hundreds of small creatures
run around inside.

00:03:20.569 --> 00:03:25.570
They bring the vase secured in the containment
pod back to the SCP Foundation site where

00:03:25.570 --> 00:03:27.250
it can be studied further.

00:03:27.250 --> 00:03:32.260
It is transferred to a containment chamber
where it is observed by Light and Voux.

00:03:32.260 --> 00:03:38.280
After a few days, SCP-019 slows the manifestation
rate of the SCP-019-2 creatures.

00:03:38.280 --> 00:03:43.819
When the vase was first secured, agents were
ordered to shoot the creatures on sight, but

00:03:43.819 --> 00:03:49.190
the number of bullets being used was unreasonable,
so they resorted to flame-throwers.

00:03:49.190 --> 00:03:54.790
The doctors decide the best course of action
is to put SCP-019 into a room hooked up to

00:03:54.790 --> 00:03:56.180
an incinerator.

00:03:56.180 --> 00:04:00.480
This way if too many creatures are manifested,
they can all be burnt to a crisp with the

00:04:00.480 --> 00:04:01.770
push of a button.

00:04:01.770 --> 00:04:05.570
Dr. Voux can’t help but think that this
must have been what Captain Kirk felt like

00:04:05.570 --> 00:04:09.319
on the starship Enterprise when it became
infested with Tribbles.

00:04:09.319 --> 00:04:15.420
Eventually, it is discovered that as long
as SCP-019 is kept at zero degrees Celsius,

00:04:15.420 --> 00:04:20.900
and no one goes near it, the object only manifests
one creature per hour.

00:04:20.900 --> 00:04:27.240
This is much easier to manage than the hordes
of SCP-019-2 instances that came out of the

00:04:27.240 --> 00:04:29.110
vase previously.

00:04:29.110 --> 00:04:34.439
Doctors Light and Vaux observe and collect
data on SCP-019 through a glass viewport that

00:04:34.439 --> 00:04:36.849
looks into its containment chamber.

00:04:36.849 --> 00:04:42.069
The incinerator is turned on at least once
every 24 hours just to clear the room of creatures.

00:04:42.069 --> 00:04:48.229
When they are not working with the vase itself
the doctors examine SCP-019-2 entities to

00:04:48.229 --> 00:04:51.439
try and understand what they are and what
they want.

00:04:51.439 --> 00:04:55.400
They capture one of the creatures and put
it in a reinforced pen.

00:04:55.400 --> 00:04:59.590
Light and Vaux provide the specimen with live
chickens for food and as much water as the

00:04:59.590 --> 00:05:00.930
creature can drink.

00:05:00.930 --> 00:05:06.849
The noises that SCP-019-2 makes sounds like
muffled sets of words.

00:05:06.849 --> 00:05:11.270
When linguists are brought in they determine
that the vocalizations are phonetically similar

00:05:11.270 --> 00:05:13.789
to Ancient Hellenic languages.

00:05:13.789 --> 00:05:18.289
This is consistent with what was spoken at
the ancient Greek city where the ceramic vase

00:05:18.289 --> 00:05:19.490
was found.

00:05:19.490 --> 00:05:22.559
The doctors give the specimen a series of
puzzles to solve.

00:05:22.559 --> 00:05:25.639
It can make its way through a maze to find
a piece of chicken.

00:05:25.639 --> 00:05:33.460
But when it is given opportunities to show
its sentience, SCP-019-2 always falls short.

00:05:33.460 --> 00:05:37.930
Doctor Light and Doctor Vaux determine the
creatures are about as intelligent as lab

00:05:37.930 --> 00:05:38.930
rats.

00:05:38.930 --> 00:05:46.370
One of the most peculiar things is that SCP-019-2
instances only live for less than 48 hours.

00:05:46.370 --> 00:05:51.259
No matter how much food, water, or care is
given to the creatures they drop dead in a

00:05:51.259 --> 00:05:53.999
day or two after being manifested.

00:05:53.999 --> 00:05:58.470
Doctor Light moves one of the dead critters
to an operating room where it can be dissected.

00:05:58.470 --> 00:06:03.160
She cuts down the middle of its stomach with
a scalpel and peels the skin and muscle away.

00:06:03.160 --> 00:06:07.719
“Well, that explains that,” she says to
the other researchers standing in the room.

00:06:07.719 --> 00:06:13.639
“The muscles seem to degrade rapidly from
the instant SCP-019-2 is manifested into our

00:06:13.639 --> 00:06:14.639
world.

00:06:14.639 --> 00:06:18.469
There is basically no digestive tract other
than a mouth and throat, but the most surprising

00:06:18.469 --> 00:06:21.550
thing is the complete lack of internal organs.”

00:06:21.550 --> 00:06:25.539
Doctor Vaux pushes the intercom button from
the viewing room in which he is observing

00:06:25.539 --> 00:06:26.539
the procedure.

00:06:26.539 --> 00:06:29.539
“What do you mean there are no internal
organs?

00:06:29.539 --> 00:06:33.470
It must have some sort of brain and cardiovascular
system.”

00:06:33.470 --> 00:06:36.860
“Yeah, but that’s about it,” Doctor
Light responds.

00:06:36.860 --> 00:06:41.300
“There appears to be a very simple central
nervous system with a brain the size of a

00:06:41.300 --> 00:06:43.849
pea, and a heart, but nothing else.

00:06:43.849 --> 00:06:48.180
This creature can’t metabolize the food
it eats or filter out toxins, and I have no

00:06:48.180 --> 00:06:49.939
idea how it breathes.

00:06:49.939 --> 00:06:51.339
We need to run more tests.”

00:06:51.339 --> 00:06:55.149
With each new specimen that’s examined the
results are the same.

00:06:55.149 --> 00:06:59.930
The creatures aren’t very intelligent, they
die in under 48 hours, and they lack pretty

00:06:59.930 --> 00:07:02.150
much any internal organs.

00:07:02.150 --> 00:07:05.539
Then one day everything changes for the worst.

00:07:05.539 --> 00:07:11.029
The guard posted to watch over SCP-019 notes
something strange occurred during his shift.

00:07:11.029 --> 00:07:18.560
Without fail, the vase manifests an instance
of SCP-019-2 every hour, but around 3:00 AM,

00:07:18.560 --> 00:07:22.119
no creature was generated, or at least that’s
what appeared to happen.

00:07:22.119 --> 00:07:27.069
The guard puts on protective equipment and
enters the room to get a closer look, but

00:07:27.069 --> 00:07:28.309
there is nothing there.

00:07:28.309 --> 00:07:33.809
He locks up, records the anomaly, and returns
to the viewing glass to continue his watch.

00:07:33.809 --> 00:07:38.809
Over the next hour the vase manifests a creature
as if everything is back to normal.

00:07:38.809 --> 00:07:43.060
The next day, Light and Vaux arrive at work
to find everything in chaos.

00:07:43.060 --> 00:07:46.050
The power in different sections of the facility
is failing.

00:07:46.050 --> 00:07:50.159
It is as if something has gotten into the
ducts and is chewing through the wiring.

00:07:50.159 --> 00:07:54.960
A team of agents uses thermal imaging devices
to track down the entity that is causing all

00:07:54.960 --> 00:07:56.050
the mayhem.

00:07:56.050 --> 00:07:57.870
They bring it back to the research lab.

00:07:57.870 --> 00:08:01.830
“Take a look at this,” the agent says
pointing at an empty operating table.

00:08:01.830 --> 00:08:04.839
He hands Doctor Light his thermal imaging
goggles.

00:08:04.839 --> 00:08:08.400
Without them, there appears to be nothing
on the table, but when she looks through the

00:08:08.400 --> 00:08:12.099
device, she can see an instance of SCP-019-2.

00:08:12.099 --> 00:08:15.759
“My God,” Doctor Light whispers.

00:08:15.759 --> 00:08:16.779
“They’re evolving.”

00:08:16.779 --> 00:08:22.909
The creature is exactly the same as all the
others except this one is invisible.

00:08:22.909 --> 00:08:27.389
Suddenly an alarm goes off and red warning
lights turn on across the facility.

00:08:27.389 --> 00:08:29.539
Light rips off the goggles and looks at Doctor
Vaux.

00:08:29.539 --> 00:08:31.770
“We need to get back to the vase now!”

00:08:31.770 --> 00:08:32.770
she yells.

00:08:32.770 --> 00:08:35.610
They sprint out of the operating room and
down the hall.

00:08:35.610 --> 00:08:40.370
As they turn the corner they hear gunshots
and the spray of fire from flame-throwers.

00:08:40.370 --> 00:08:45.519
On the other side of the corridor where SCP-019
is contained, there are agents battling with

00:08:45.519 --> 00:08:50.160
thousands of instances of SCP-019-2.

00:08:50.160 --> 00:08:55.180
The flame-throwers that had been so effective
at killing the creatures now appear useless.

00:08:55.180 --> 00:09:00.529
It is as if the creatures have evolved some
sort of protective skin to combat the flames.

00:09:00.529 --> 00:09:02.699
“Oh no,” gasps Doctor Light.

00:09:02.699 --> 00:09:04.270
“We’ve gotta get out of here!”

00:09:04.270 --> 00:09:09.019
She grabs Doctor Vaux’s shoulder and drags
him with her as she runs down the hall.

00:09:09.019 --> 00:09:11.050
Behind them, the screams of agents can be
heard.

00:09:11.050 --> 00:09:16.870
They are quickly muffled as thousands upon
thousands of SCP-019-2 creatures overwhelm

00:09:16.870 --> 00:09:17.870
them.

00:09:17.870 --> 00:09:20.210
Light glances behind her to see what is happening.

00:09:20.210 --> 00:09:23.630
What she finds is a wall of creatures rushing
towards her.

00:09:23.630 --> 00:09:25.480
There must be millions now.

00:09:25.480 --> 00:09:31.130
It seems like SCP-019 was tired of being contained
by the Foundation and has sent an invasion

00:09:31.130 --> 00:09:32.990
force to escape its captors.

00:09:32.990 --> 00:09:34.570
“We’re not going to make it!”

00:09:34.570 --> 00:09:35.769
Vaux yells.

00:09:35.769 --> 00:09:37.870
He stumbles and falls to the ground.

00:09:37.870 --> 00:09:41.050
Doctor Light skids to a stop and turns to
go back for him.

00:09:41.050 --> 00:09:42.230
But it’s too late.

00:09:42.230 --> 00:09:45.709
The wave of SCP-019-2 is closing in.

00:09:45.709 --> 00:09:50.500
She watches in horror as Doctor Vaux is consumed
by the mass of creatures.

00:09:50.500 --> 00:09:53.209
She turns and continues to run.

00:09:53.209 --> 00:09:54.920
The exit is in sight.

00:09:54.920 --> 00:09:57.019
Doctor Light makes a dash towards the door.

00:09:57.019 --> 00:10:00.399
She can feel the tiny feet of the creatures
clawing at her heels.

00:10:00.399 --> 00:10:05.040
She gives it everything she’s got and accelerates,
putting some distance between her and the

00:10:05.040 --> 00:10:09.190
millions of SCP-019-2 entities.

00:10:09.190 --> 00:10:13.290
Doctor Light slams through the exit door and
immediately closes it behind her.

00:10:13.290 --> 00:10:16.360
She manages to slide the metal locking bar
into place.

00:10:16.360 --> 00:10:20.829
The impact from the wave of creatures against
the door sends her stumbling backward.

00:10:20.829 --> 00:10:22.209
She is safe now.

00:10:22.209 --> 00:10:26.529
As Light lays on the ground panting and staring
at the door she thinks to herself.

00:10:26.529 --> 00:10:30.420
Well, they’ll all be dead in a couple of
days and then we can try again.

00:10:30.420 --> 00:10:34.000
Now watch “SCP-001 - Which is the Real 001?

00:10:34.000 --> 00:10:35.870
(SCP Animation).”

00:10:35.870 --> 00:10:39.670
Or check out “SCP-823 - Carnival of Horrors
(SCP Animation).”

